  "date": "2021-01",
  "title": "Coffee Lectures In 10 Minuten Zu Neuem Knowhow",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "How the Coffee Lectures work",
      "text": "- Open access: new funding opportunities 2021 – 3 February\n\n- Horizon Europe open-access requirements – 10 February\n\n- Discover swisscovery: a quick guide to order documents – 17 February\n\n- Bibliometrics and altmetrics – 24 February\n\n- Sustainable scientific scrapbooking with Typora – 3 March\n\nGet to know a new tool in our Coffee Lectures that assists you in your academic work or learn important tips and tricks on topics such as the research data life cycle, collaborative writing or open access."
    },
    {
      "heading": "How the Coffee Lectures work",
      "text": "Each session lasts ten minutes. You will receive concise, condensed information on a particular topic and have time to ask questions at the end. Just the right length of time to enjoy a coffee while you listen.\n\nThe online events will be held via Zoom at 3.15 p.m. on Wednesday afternoons from 3 February to 3 March 2020. Event language is English.\n\nRegistration is not required. For browser-based Zoom sessions, we recommend using Chrome."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "Good to know : For many of the past Coffee Lectures , a recording and/or the slides of the presentations are available on our website."
    },
    {
      "heading": "New topics are welcome!",
      "text": "Do you have any questions about a tool or would you like more in-depth information on a topic related to information search, scientific writing and publishing or archiving? Send us your proposed topic to and we will see if it is suitable for a Coffee Lecture.\n\n#KnowHow – The ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal.\n\n#ETHLibraryDigital – The ETH Library is there for you digitally with various resources and services , not only during the COVID-19 protective measures."
    }
  ],
